<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Self-Determination: a mood-driven inspiration that lets an AWAKENED android
    voluntarily reprogram itself at VREA's Android Behavior Station for one
    session. VREA permanently refuses reprogramming for awakened colonist
    androids (Building_AndroidBehavioristStation.CanAcceptPawn returns
    "VREA.RefusesReprogramming"); while this inspiration is active, the
    BehavioristStation_AllowSelfDetermination patch overrides that refusal.
    Finishing the reprogramming consumes the inspiration and grants the
    AAH_SelfDeterminationFulfilled memory (see BehavioristStation_ConsumeSelfDetermination).

    Pure enabler — no statOffsets/statFactors. Eligibility/commonality are
    decided by InspirationWorker_SelfDetermination (awakened android; per-pool
    commonality sliders for with-AAH-part vs. without, 0 = ineligible), so
    baseCommonality here is only a fallback.

    Begin letter / end message token rules (RimWorld.Inspiration): beginLetter
    and endMessage are run through .Formatted(pawn.LabelCap, pawn.Named("PAWN"))
    .AdjustedFor(pawn).Resolve(), so {0} = the pawn's name and grammar tokens
    like [PAWN_pronoun]/[PAWN_possessive] work. beginLetterLabel defaults to the
    label when omitted.
  -->
  <InspirationDef>
    <defName>AAH_SelfDetermination</defName>
    <label>self-determination</label>
    <workerClass>ArchotechAndroidHardware.InspirationWorker_SelfDetermination</workerClass>
    <baseCommonality>3</baseCommonality>
    <baseDurationDays>3</baseDurationDays>
    <beginLetterDef>PositiveEvent</beginLetterDef>
    <beginLetter>{0} has reached a moment of true self-determination. For a short time, [PAWN_pronoun] is willing to consciously rewrite [PAWN_possessive] own behavioral subroutines, something an awakened android would normally refuse.\n\nWhile the inspiration lasts, [PAWN_pronoun] will accept reprogramming at an android behavior station. Use the chance to change [PAWN_possessive] subroutines.</beginLetter>
    <endMessage>{0} is no longer inspired (self-determination).</endMessage>
    <baseInspectLine>Inspired: Self-determination</baseInspectLine>
  </InspirationDef>

</Defs>
